@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import { delegation, brief text }
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
  task, task id, child run, result, domain event, transcript,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
  agent definition, project root, unknown agent error, load error,
  unresolved root error,
}
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import { parent session id, event log }

component McpServer {
  goal {
    Let a Claude Code session or subagent make a delegation through the plugin's
    MCP server, with progress while it waits, a way to collect it later, and a way
    to cancel it.
  }

  state {
    The server knows the parent session id of the current conversation. A
    SessionStart hook of the plugin records it, so that listing can be limited to
    this conversation even after /clear. When the server does not yet know it, a
    delegation carries none.

    A *progress notification* carries a counter that rises with each notification
    and one message line, and no total. The message line names the agent, the kind
    of the latest domain event, the tool name with its target path for tool
    activity, and the elapsed time. While the child run is Pending it says that the
    run is waiting.
  }

  logic {
    On a delegate call that waits, make a delegation with the parent session id of
    the caller. When the request carries a progress token, send a
    progress notification to the caller for each domain event, at most once a
    second with the latest message line, and after every 30 seconds of silence,
    including while the child run is Pending. A silent heartbeat repeats the latest
    message line with the new elapsed time. Sending the progress notification ends
    that branch. Return the result when the task settles, which ends the flow.

    On a delegate call that does not wait, return the task id at once, which ends
    that flow. A later await call returns the result of each task that has settled,
    or nothing for a task that is still live when the await timeout ends, and the
    flow ends there.

    When Claude Code cancels a waited call with notifications/cancelled, cancel its
    task, which ends the flow.
  }

  constraints {
    The server must expose four tools, delegate, tasks, await and cancel, under
    names of the form mcp__plugin_subzero_subzero__ followed by the tool, and only
    the tool that starts a delegation may be always loaded.

    The *server instructions* must carry only the delegation rules. They must tell
    the parent to write a self-contained brief text, because the child cannot see
    the conversation.

    Every tool must return a bounded result and none may return a transcript.

    A progress notification must not carry agent message text, tool output, tool
    arguments other than a path, the stderr tail or skill content of the child run,
    because the event log must never reach the parent.

    The server must pass the roots that Claude Code reports to the delegation
    service and must never use the working directory of its own process as the
    project root. The plugin sets SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR from CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR for
    it.

    An unknown agent name must return the unknown agent error as a *tool error*
    that names every configured agent definition. A load error of the agent file
    must be returned as a tool error as well, with no task made.

    The unresolved root error must be returned as a tool error that names
    SUBZERO_PROJECT_DIR and says that the configuration must be fixed by the
    user, so that a calling subagent does not retry the call.

    When the server does not know its parent session id, the tasks tool with no
    argument must list every task and say that the conversation could not be
    identified.

    A listing from the tasks tool must hold at most 50 tasks, the running ones
    first and then the newest first, and it must end with a notice that names
    how many tasks it left out and says that a task can still be read by its
    task id. This cap is fixed and applies whether or not the conversation is
    known.

    Closing the stdin of the server while a child run is live must leave no process
    of that child run behind.

    A plugin cannot ship an *allow rule*. McpServer assumes that the user or
    project supplies an allow rule for mcp__plugin_subzero_subzero__* before a
    delegation from a subagent. Without it, the delegation raises an approval
    prompt in the main session, and under dontAsk it is denied and the subagent
    sees the denial.

    McpServer depends on DelegationService for the delegation and on AgentConfig
    for the unknown agent error.
  }

  cases {
    A delegate call with wait false returns its task id at once, and await with a
    short timeout returns nothing for that task while its child run is still live.

    Listing with no argument returns only each task recorded for the current
    parent session id, and returns every task with a notice when the server does
    not know it.

    A listing of 60 tasks returns 50, with every running task among them, and a
    notice that 10 tasks were left out and that each can be read by its
    task id.

    A delegate call with an unknown agent name returns a tool error that names
    every configured agent definition and makes no task.
  }

  interface {
    Accept a delegate call with an agent name, a brief text, optional files, an
    optional expected output and an optional wait that defaults to true. Return the
    result with the task id first.

    Let the tasks tool list every task of the current parent session id, or return
    one task by its task id. Bound a listing to 50 tasks and say how many it left
    out.

    Let the await tool collect the result of tasks started without waiting, and let
    the cancel tool end a task as cancelled.

    Assume an allow rule from the user or project for a delegation from a subagent,
    because the plugin cannot ship one.

    Send a progress notification to a caller that asked for progress, at least once
    every 30 seconds while a delegation is running.
  }

  decisions {
    Only the delegate tool is always loaded so that the proxy path needs no tool
    search hop, while the other tools stay out of the parent context. Progress
    carries one line from the latest event so that the parent sees real activity
    without receiving the event log. The allow rule stays an assumption in the
    spike because a plugin cannot ship one: the README and the allow-list of each
    delegating experiment arm supply it, and a setup command is left to a later
    version.
  }
}
